{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794378635036,"sessionID":"ses_e36c0300cffeuhOocOqdZKOL18","part":{"id":"prt_1c94d16fb0015K46YfK2YP1YMh","messageID":"msg_1c94cde0b001l87yRTlp7z7ubK","sessionID":"ses_e36c0300cffeuhOocOqdZKOL18","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794378635036,"sessionID":"ses_e36c0300cffeuhOocOqdZKOL18","part":{"id":"prt_1c94d16fe001FhgUPINJNauTj4","messageID":"msg_1c94cde0b001l87yRTlp7z7ubK","sessionID":"ses_e36c0300cffeuhOocOqdZKOL18","type":"text","text":"Done. Summary of the build:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) — Flask + stdlib SQLite at `data/app.db` (created on startup, survives restarts):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201, 409 on duplicate), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 `{\"token\"}`), plus `GET /api/auth/me` for session restore. Tokens are signed (itsdangerous) and sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; protected routes answer 401 otherwise.\n- `GET /api/tracks` (`q`/`page`/`page_size`, newest first → `{\"items\", \"total\", \"page\", \"page_size\"}`), `POST /api/tracks` (201, rejects non-http/https urls), `GET /api/tracks/{id}`, `DELETE /api/tracks/{id}` (204, 403 unless owner), `POST /api/tracks/{id}/plays` (public, increments and returns the track).\n- Track objects carry exactly `id, title, artist, url, duration, play_count, created_at, added_by`; errors are `{\"error\": \"...\"}`. The catch-all serves `frontend/dist` with SPA fallback but returns JSON 404 for unknown `/api/*` paths.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`) — React 19 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind v4 (only `src/index.css` with `@import \"tailwindcss\"`):\n- `AuthPanel` register/sign-in forms, header shows signed-in username + sign out (`src/components/AuthPanel.tsx`).\n- `TrackList` with title/artist/duration/plays, search, paging, and delete-with-`window.confirm` on own tracks (`src/components/TrackList.tsx`).\n- `PlayerBar` with play/pause, seek, volume, current title/artist, next/prev (`src/components/PlayerBar.tsx`); playback is driven by an `<audio>` element in `src/App.tsx`, which calls `POST /plays` when a track starts and auto-advances on end.\n- `AddTrackForm` renders the API's validation messages (`src/components/AddTrackForm.tsx`).\n\n**Verified**: 65-check Flask test-client suite (auth, validation, paging, search, plays, ownership), `tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build`, SSR render smoke, and a live gunicorn run from a clean `data/` covering health, register/login, add/list/delete, play counting, and static serving.","time":{"start":1794378635006,"end":1794378635011}}}
